# Phase 7: suffixes in expressions (render::read::unlift, `Rd::write_for`):
# a number inside an expression is respelled in the target's suffixes
# where the target's reader would read its spelling as another value or
# as no number, as a standalone value already is (Spectre `2*1M`, 2 mega,
# was written for ngspice as `2*1M`, 2 milli). Every line below keeps its
# value; none of the corpora holds a Spectre `M` or a SPICE `meg` inside
# an expression crossing dialects. Per set: ltspice 9, xyce 4.
ltspice/ltspice_demos/LT3724.net cdl {.001µ/5} is {1n/5}: ngspice's reader has no µ (was {.001u/5}, µ replaced as text)
ltspice/ltspice_demos/LTC3125_DC1267A.net cdl {2200µ/20} is {2.2m/20}: ngspice's reader has no µ (was {2200u/20})
ltspice/ltspice_demos/LTC3452.net cdl {.1µ/5} is {100n/5}: ngspice's reader has no µ (was {.1u/5})
ltspice/ltspice_demos/LTC3606B.net cdl {2200µ/10} is {2.2m/10}: ngspice's reader has no µ (was {2200u/10})
ltspice/ltspice_demos/LTC3619B_DC1489A.net cdl {2200µ/10} is {2.2m/10}: ngspice's reader has no µ (was {2200u/10})
ltspice/ltspice_demos/LTC3835-1_LT3580.net cdl {0.01µ/10} is {10n/10} (twice): ngspice's reader has no µ (was {0.01u/10})
ltspice/ltspice_examples/3705.net cdl {.047µ/5} and {.018µ/2.5} are {47n/5} and {18n/2.5}: ngspice's reader has no µ
ltspice/ltspice_examples/3724.net cdl {.0015µ/10} is {1.5n/10}: ngspice's reader has no µ (was {.0015u/10})
ltspice/ltspice_examples/3800.net cdl {.0015µ/10} is {1.5n/10}: ngspice's reader has no µ (was {.0015u/10})
xyce/PARAMS2/Params_C4.cir spectre ISmant*1F is ISmant*1f: Xyce's F is femto (case-blind), Spectre's scales are case-sensitive and have no F
xyce/PARAMS2/Params_C4_hs.cir spectre ISmant*1F is ISmant*1f: Xyce's F is femto (case-blind), Spectre's scales are case-sensitive and have no F
xyce/PARAMS2/Params_C5.cir spectre a `real` function's `return 1F*X` is `return 1f*X`: Spectre has no F scale
xyce/PARAMS2/Params_C5_hs.cir spectre a `real` function's `return 1F*X` is `return 1f*X`: Spectre has no F scale

# Phase 7: named-write: .print and .save on Spectre (render::named::bench).
# A .print's signals are a Spectre save (Spectre Reference 5.0 p.886:
# nodes and inst:terminal currents), its voltage views (vdb, a difference)
# the post-processor's; an output with no signal form (an expression,
# format=) is noted W0023. A device current is inst:1, the first terminal
# by index (p.886), not :p (a resistor's terminals are 1 2, p.629); a
# subcircuit node keeps its hierarchy (x1.n, Xyce's X1:n), each segment
# escaped, not x1\.n (one name). Per set: xyce 1390, spice-bench 4.
