# Phase 7: named-write: behavioural sources on Spectre (render::named::bsource).
# A B source (and E value=, G cur=) is a Spectre bsource v=/i= (Spectre
# Reference 5.0 pp.856-860), its expression written from the tree with
# every compound operand parenthesised: v() as written, i(V1) as
# i("v1:0"), time $time, temper temp, pi M_PI, ln log; ngspice's x**y,
# x^y, pow(x,y) as pow(abs(x),y) (ngspice-45 computes |x|^y). An
# expression with no Spectre form (hertz, u(), Xyce's log, another
# dialect's power) stays W0102; a Laplace source is W0011. Refused before,
# written now. Per set: xyce 93, spice-bench 6.
spice-bench/ngspice/examples/various/FFT_Leakage.sp spectre a behavioural source written as a Spectre bsource
