# Phase 7: named-write: analyses (render::named::bench, vacask_bench).
# Spectre: a nested .dc is a sweep around the inner dc (SPICE's first source
# innermost; Spectre Reference 19.1 pp.406-409); an oct sweep is ngspice's
# grid (acan.c: f *= 2^(1/n) while f <= stop + 2^(1/n)*stop*reltol) as
# values=[...] (p.43: Spectre has no oct); .tf is xf values=[0] (pp.438-439),
# its input/output resistances noted W0125. VACASK: a one-point sweep
# (.dc v 5 5 1, .ac lin 1 f f) is points=0 (lib/answeep.cpp
# setupLinearSweep: end = points+1). Refused before, written now, except
# the .tf lines (xf freq=0 before). Per set: spice-bench 1584 + 1, xyce 207 + 105.
spice-bench/cmcqa/gf180/gf180_beta_vnpn_0p54x16_14.sp spectre a nested .dc as a sweep, an oct sweep as values, .tf as xf values=[0]
spice-bench/cmcqa/gf180/gf180_beta_vnpn_0p54x16_2.sp spectre a nested .dc as a sweep, an oct sweep as values, .tf as xf values=[0]
