# Phase 7: spectre-read: masters with a SPICE card (render::read::named_masters).
# A Spectre `iprobe` is a 0 V source, `port` ngspice's RF port (the source
# behind `r` twice `dc`/`mag`, [CMP] p.602), a lossless `tline` a T line,
# a `bsource` with `v=`/`i=` over v(), $time and the functions both define
# a B source ([CMP] pp.856-859); each was a statement kept as text. The
# Spectre writer of a B source is gap-named-write's (W0102 here until it
# merges). Per set: fixtures 2 (one input).
fixtures/tests/fixtures/transpiler/f1.scs spectre b1, b2, b3 now B sources written back as bsource v=/i= (gap-named-write's writer); were Spectre text copied as written (W0027)
fixtures/tests/fixtures/transpiler/f1.scs cdl b1, b2, b3 now B cards (B1 a b V=v(a,b)*2 …) among the elements; were Spectre text copied after them

# Phase 7: spectre-read: analyses (render::read::named_bench, `Ana::Spectre`).
# A Spectre `name master … {` analysis is read, not kept as a block: a
# `montecarlo` over one analysis is `Ana::MonteCarlo` (Spectre writes it
# after the deck's other analyses, its body indented as read; VACASK its
# `mc` loop, or W0115), any other Spectre-only analysis `Ana::Spectre`
# (Spectre writes it as read; elsewhere W0015 where the target has no such
# analysis, W0001 where it has one not translated). CDL no longer copies
# the analysis as text. Per set: fixtures 18 (five inputs, the T-S decks).
fixtures/tests/spectre/t_s2_agauss.scs spectre the montecarlo block written after op1 dc (the bench's order), its body indented as read; was a block kept in place
